<SubSection title="Buoyancy" id="Buoyancy">
<p>Cores inside molds float because molten metal is typically denser. The buoyant force is:</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="F_b = \\rho_{\\text{metal}} V g" title="" />

<p>and core weight is:</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="F_g = \\rho_{\\text{core}} V g" title="" />

<p>Chaplets must resist:</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="F_{\\text{top}} = F_b - F_g" title="" />

<h4><strong>Bottom Chaplet Force (Prior to Filling)</strong></h4>
<p>Before pouring, no buoyant force exists. The bottom chaplets must therefore support the entire weight of the core:</p> 


<DisplayEquation equation="F_{\\text{bottom, prior}} = F_g = \\rho_{\\text{core}} V g" title="" />

<hr />
</SubSection>
<SubSubSection title="Example Problem: Number of Chaplets Required" id="Example Problem: Number of Chaplets Required">
<p><strong>Question: </strong>Determine how many chaplets are needed to hold the core in place.</p>
<em>Image</em>
<p>Given:</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="\\rho_{\\text{metal}} = 2.7,\\ \\rho_{\\text{core}} = 0.9,\\ V = 4\\text{ cm}^3" title="" />


<DisplayEquation equation="g=9.81,\\quad F_{\\text{chaplet}} = 0.01\\text{ N}" title="" />

<strong>Solution:</strong>

<DisplayEquation equation="F_g = 0.9(4)(9.81) = 0.035\\text{ N}" title="" />


<DisplayEquation equation="F_b = 2.7(4)(9.81) = 0.106\\text{ N}" title="" />


<DisplayEquation equation="F_{\\text{top}} = 0.071\\text{ N}" title="" />

<p>Chaplets needed:</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="\\text{Top} = \\lceil 0.071/0.01 \\rceil = 8" title="" />


<DisplayEquation equation="\\text{Bottom} = \\lceil 0.035/0.01 \\rceil = 4" title="" />
</SubSubSection>

